name = "SAEF Toolbox - Antistasi Ultimate Integration";
author = "SAEF";
tooltip = "SAEF features for the Antistasi Ultimate campaign";

// One physical line: mod.cpp strings cannot span lines. <br/> and <t> are rendered by
// the Arma 3 Launcher.
description = "SAEF-specific features for the Antistasi Ultimate campaign server.<br/><br/>The Antistasi mission ships inside @AntistasiUltimate's own PBO and cannot be edited, so anything a normal SAEF mission would put in its init scripts has to be pushed in from outside. That is what this mod does.<br/><br/><t size='1.1'>SAEF rebel identity</t><br/>Replaces the Aegis FIA rebel faction's name, flag and strategic map marker with the SAEF patch - on the faction-select screen, on in-game flagpoles, and on the map. Everything else about the faction (equipment, vehicles, loadouts) is left exactly as Antistasi defines it.<br/><br/><t size='1.1'>Wave respawn</t><br/>Optional. Holds dead players in spectator and releases them together in waves, instead of Antistasi's flat 15 second respawn. Driven by the SAEF Toolbox respawn handler and configured from the mission setup screen under EXTENDER OPTIONS: minimum and maximum wait, how long respawn stays open, how many dead players force a wave early, and an optional penalty added per death. Editable mid-campaign; changes apply within a few seconds. Disabled by default.<br/><br/><t size='1.1'>Admin utilities</t><br/>Log StatTrack, Become Invincible and Become Vulnerable, under ACE self-interact > Tools > Admin Utilities > Mission Utilities. Visible only to a logged-in admin - regular players never see them.<br/><br/><t size='1.1'>Requirements</t><br/>@AntistasiUltimate, @SAEFToolbox and CBA_A3. ACE for the admin actions.<br/><br/><t size='1.1'>Installing</t><br/>Needed on the server and in the player preset. The flag textures and the map marker class are rendered client-side, so a player without this mod sees the vanilla FIA flag and a broken marker lookup. The two script PBOs are server-guarded and do nothing on a client, so shipping the whole folder to everyone is safe.";
